00:04:52,334 --> 00:04:54,464
I don't know how to use this.

457
00:04:54,884 --> 00:04:57,054
It predates the internet,

458
00:04:57,054 --> 00:04:59,764
so I can't hook it up to anything.

459
00:05:00,014 --> 00:05:02,344
For now, I'll need these parts.

460
00:05:03,094 --> 00:05:04,354
You heard the man.

461
00:05:04,354 --> 00:05:06,014
Take care of it, assistant.

462
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:09,184
I'd like you to stop talking to me like that.

463
00:05:09,184 --> 00:05:10,394
You're my assistant.

464
00:05:10,394 --> 00:05:11,734
No, I'm not!

465
00:05:11,734 --> 00:05:13,774
Okarin, you go.

466
00:05:13,774 --> 00:05:16,194
Miss Makise probably doesn't know Akiba.

467
00:05:16,944 --> 00:05:18,154
Very well.

468
00:05:18,154 --> 00:05:19,034
Mayuri, let's go!

469
00:05:19,284 --> 00:05:23,614
Mayushii will do her best to show Kurisu-chan around the lab,

470
00:05:23,614 --> 00:05:25,914
so she'll like it!

471
00:05:25,914 --> 00:05:27,374
So, I'll stay here.

472
00:05:27,374 --> 00:05:29,334
Christina, you...

473
00:05:29,334 --> 00:05:31,374
You couldn't have entrapped Mayuri with your wiles, as wellâ

474
00:05:31,374 --> 00:05:32,294
I did no such thing!

475
00:05:32,294 --> 00:05:34,174
Miss Makise seducing Mayuri...

476
00:05:34,724 --> 00:05:36,384
Yuri is in the air...

477
00:05:36,384 --> 00:05:37,754
Don't imagine that, pervert!

478
00:05:38,174 --> 00:05:40,764
It's nice for girls to be together, isn't it?

479
00:05:41,134 --> 00:05:44,014
Anyway, why don't you show me around?

480
00:05:44,014 --> 00:05:44,844
Okay!

481
00:05:45,264 --> 00:05:48,604
We'll start with the shower room.

482
00:05:50,024 --> 00:05:51,564
It has a shower...

483
00:05:52,894 --> 00:05:57,314
But sometimes, if you use it for too long, 
the water gets cold. So be careful!

484
00:05:57,984 --> 00:06:02,244
You use this sometimes?

485
00:06:02,244 --> 00:06:03,744
Yeah, once in a while.

486
00:06:04,164 --> 00:06:07,124
Please promise me you'll never use the shower here again!

487
00:06:07,124 --> 00:06:08,914
It's too dangerous!

488
00:06:07,584 --> 00:06:08,914
Don't look at me.

489
00:06:09,204 --> 00:06:10,244
It's suicide.

490
00:06:10,244 --> 00:06:13,334
Actually, what are you doing here anyway?

491
00:06:13,334 --> 00:06:14,624
Did he threaten or blackmail

492
00:06:14,624 --> 00:06:17,084
you into becoming a member, against your will?

493
00:06:17,754 --> 00:06:20,344
Mayushii is Okarin's hostage.

494
00:06:24,134 --> 00:06:26,554
I should call the police.

495
00:06:25,474 --> 00:06:26,554
Wait!

496
00:06:26,554 --> 00:06:28,604
She just said she was your hostage.

497
00:06:28,604 --> 00:06:29,764
That's real evidence.

498
00:06:29,764 --> 00:06:31,274
Nope.

499
00:06:32,224 --> 00:06:36,274
Mayushii became a hostage herself!

500
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,484
What does that mean?

501
00:06:40,194 --> 00:06:41,404
I'm going.

502
00:06:41,404 --> 00:06:43,194
Bye!

503
00:06:45,654 --> 00:06:49,494
This should work as a replacement, I'm pretty sure...

504
00:06:49,494 --> 00:06:50,914
Yo!

505
00:06:51,384 --> 00:06:53,454
Think you'll be able to use that IBN 5100?

506
00:06:54,124 --> 00:06:56,174
Don't say that name here!

507
00:06:57,544 --> 00:06:59,004
Collecting parts?

508
00:06:59,504 --> 00:07:00,884
Want some help?

509
00:07:02,344 --> 00:07:04,014
I didn't expect a part-time warrior

510
00:07:04,014 --> 00:07:06,344
to be so knowledgeable about PCs.

511
00:07:06,344 --> 00:07:10,144
I once knew someone who understood a lot about IBNs.

512
00:07:11,014 --> 00:07:12,104
Really?

513
00:07:12,104 --> 00:07:13,724
I'd like you to put me in touch with them!

514
00:07:14,604 --> 00:07:15,434
It's impossible.

515
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:19,654
If you refuse, you'll experience the worst hell this world has to offer!

516
00:07:19,654 --> 00:07:21,194
I said it's impossible.

517
00:07:21,194 --> 00:07:22,904
Don't you value your life?

518
00:07:22,904 --> 00:07:25,744
He's dead.

519
00:07:26,704 --> 00:07:28,244
He died years ago.

520
00:07:29,374 --> 00:07:30,494
I'm sorry.

521
00:07:31,494 --> 00:07:34,254
No, I apologize for earlier.

522
00:07:34,754 --> 00:07:36,414
Did my assistant do something to you?

523
00:07:37,974 --> 00:07:38,964
Nothing.

524
00:07:38,964 --> 00:07:41,004
Like maybe she glared at you first...

525
00:07:41,004 --> 00:07:43,304
I know, she snorted at you!

526
00:07:43,804 --> 00:07:44,964
No.

527
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:46,764
She hasn't done anything.

528
00:07:46,764 --> 00:07:48,304
Then...

529
00:07:50,604 --> 00:07:54,814
She doesn't know anything yet.

530
00:07:56,484 --> 00:07:59,354
But be wary of her.

531
00:07:59,354 --> 00:08:00,604
What do you mean?

532
00:08:04,384 --> 00:08:05,534
Bombs?

533
00:08:07,484 --> 00:08:08,974
They're broadcasting the fireworks.

534
00:08:09,324 --> 00:08:10,914
Those are today, I think.

535
00:08:10,914 --> 00:08:13,664
Fireworks... Fireworks...

536
00:08:13,664 --> 00:08:15,244
I've heard of those!

537
00:08:16,584 --> 00:08:17,834
You've never seen any?

538
00:08:17,834 --> 00:08:19,424
Where are they? Which way?

539
00:08:20,874 --> 00:08:22,294
Go out that way, toward the river,

540
00:08:22,294 --> 00:08:23,964
and you should be able to see them.

541
00:08:24,254 --> 00:08:25,004
Thanks!

542
00:08:29,264 --> 00:08:31,594
Tell me your mail address.

543
00:08:33,644 --> 00:08:34,514
A festival?

544
00:08:34,814 --> 00:08:36,934
Fireworks!

545
00:08:39,394 --> 00:08:40,774
Fireworks, huh?

546
00:08:40,774 --> 00:08:41,944
Do you want to go?

547
00:08:43,174 --> 00:08:44,484
Not really...

548
00:08:45,004 --> 00:08:45,944
Okarin!

549
00:08:49,324 --> 00:08:50,204
Heading home?

550
00:08:51,074 --> 00:08:52,324
Did you find the parts?

551
00:08:52,324 --> 00:08:54,034
I've got them all right here.

552
00:08:54,034 --> 00:08:54,874
I see...

553
00:08:54,874 --> 00:08:57,664
So you're going to start trying things.

554
00:08:58,204 --> 00:08:59,754
Interested?

555
00:09:00,914 --> 00:09:02,044
You are, aren't you?

556
00:09:02,044 --> 00:09:04,634
Just a little, all right?

557
00:09:04,634 --> 00:09:06,304
But I'm not interested

558
00:09:06,304 --> 00:09:08,634
in that SERN conspiracy nonsense.

559
00:09:09,054 --> 00:09:11,594
I just want to know the truth.

560
00:09:12,264 --> 00:09:13,094
I'm sorry.

561
00:09:13,094 --> 00:09:13,684
What? What?

562
00:09:13,684 --> 00:09:16,184
I'm heading back to the lab.

563
00:09:16,184 --> 00:09:17,264
I see.

564
00:09:17,264 --> 00:09:19,144
Then Mayushii is going home.

565
00:09:19,144 --> 00:09:19,934
Okay.

566
00:09:22,354 --> 00:09:23,404
Kurisu-chan?

567
00:09:23,404 --> 00:09:23,904
Yes?

568
00:09:23,904 --> 00:09:25,984
You'll come back, right?

569
00:09:26,444 --> 00:09:27,114
Yeah.

570
00:09:27,524 --> 00:09:30,154
I'm a member until I return to America.

571
00:09:30,494 --> 00:09:31,494
Yeah!

572
00:09:32,204 --> 00:09:33,534
Bye!

573
00:09:33,994 --> 00:09:35,744
What was that?

574
00:09:36,164 --> 00:09:37,164
You're my assistant.

575
00:09:37,164 --> 00:09:39,164
Of course you're going to the lab.

576
00:09:40,794 --> 00:09:43,294
She said you're childhood friends.

577
00:09:43,294 --> 00:09:45,174
How did you grow up

578
00:09:45,174 --> 00:09:47,964
in the same environment, and end up this socially awkward?

579
00:09:48,334 --> 00:09:51,594
Mayuri's always been a bit of a weird one...

580
00:09:51,594 --> 00:09:53,224
I was talking to you!

581
00:09:55,934 --> 00:09:57,404
Part-Time Warrior

582
00:09:55,934 --> 00:09:57,404
First Message

583
00:09:55,934 --> 00:09:57,404
More than I imagined! 
Fireworks are great!

584
00:09:56,184 --> 00:09:57,894
First Message.

585
00:09:57,894 --> 00:09:59,474
More than I imagined!

586
00:09:59,474 --> 00:10:01,434
Fireworks are great!

587
00:10:10,324 --> 00:10:11,744
It never worked after that, huh?

588
00:10:12,284 --> 00:10:13,704
I'm borrowing this.

589
00:10:16,454 --> 00:10:19,544
Lab coats always calm me down.

590
00:10:20,744 --> 00:10:21,754
Perfect!

591
00:10:22,374 --> 00:10:24,254
I was right...

592
00:10:24,754 --> 00:10:26,134
You're perfect.

593
00:10:26,464 --> 00:10:28,094
Wh-What's wrong?

594
00:10:28,094 --> 00:10:29,214
You're creeping me out.

595
00:10:29,214 --> 00:10:30,424
A lab coat!

596
00:10:30,424 --> 00:10:34,514
In a research organization, a lab coat is a uniform!

597
00:10:34,514 --> 00:10:35,934
I keep telling Daru and Mayuri,

598
00:10:35,934 --> 00:10:38,104
but neither of them seems to understand.

599
00:10:38,104 --> 00:10:39,814
But you understand.

600
00:10:39,814 --> 00:10:42,734
Now, let's both stand with our hands in our pockets!

601
00:10:43,864 --> 00:10:44,644
Hurry up!

602
00:10:45,064 --> 00:10:46,274
L-Like this?

603
00:10:46,274 --> 00:10:47,354
That's right!

604
00:10:47,354 --> 00:10:50,614
This is a pose of radiant intelligence, possible only for those

605
00:10:50,614 --> 00:10:52,944
who spend their lives in research!

606
00:10:52,944 --> 00:10:55,074
I give that lab coat to you.

607
00:10:55,074 --> 00:10:57,704
Let us share in the glory together...

608
00:10:59,494 --> 00:11:01,914
I really do feel like you're mocking me.

609
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:05,164
You hungry?

610
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:06,464
Shut up.

611
00:11:06,464 --> 00:11:08,214
I haven't eaten since lunch.

612
00:11:08,214 --> 00:11:09,794
Very well.

613
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:12,464
I'm in a good mood today.

614
00:11:13,924 --> 00:11:15,304
Enjoy. I demand it.

615
00:11:15,304 --> 00:11:16,054
Seriously?

616
00:11:16,054 --> 00:11:16,804
You're dissatisfied?

617
00:11:16,804 --> 00:11:18,224
Of course!

618
00:11:18,224 --> 00:11:19,684
Isn't there anything else?

619
00:11:20,064 --> 00:11:22,394
I've got some cup ramen I bought.

620
00:11:23,814 --> 00:11:25,274
But I imagine you wouldn't want it,

621
00:11:25,274 --> 00:11:26,814
as someone raised in America...

622
00:11:26,814 --> 00:11:27,944
Cup ramen?

623
00:11:29,484 --> 00:11:30,904
I'll have some cup ramen.

624
00:11:31,364 --> 00:11:32,694
What flavors?

625
00:11:32,694 --> 00:11:33,944
Soy sauce and salt!

626
00:11:36,204 --> 00:11:37,654
I'll have the salt flavor.

627
00:11:37,654 --> 00:11:39,364
And a fork.

628
00:11:43,334 --> 00:11:46,164
If you don't hurry, time will expire, and you'll lose.

629
00:11:47,504 --> 00:11:48,674
Why not give up?

630
00:11:48,674 --> 00:11:51,214
That's a virus card at the end, isn't it?

631
00:11:51,214 --> 00:11:51,964
I can tell.

632
00:11:53,054 --> 00:11:55,764
You may think that if you like.

633
00:11:55,764 --> 00:11:58,134
So I'll just put this here.

634
00:11:58,634 --> 00:12:00,804
Okay, riichi.

635
00:12:04,014 --> 00:12:07,024
You like Dr Pepper, assistant?

636
00:12:07,894 --> 00:12:10,064
I spent seven years in America, after all.

637
00:12:10,064 --> 00:12:12,904
I'd love to drink with you sometime...

638
00:12:13,344 --> 00:12:16,244
Unfortunately, I'm a minor.

639
00:12:16,244 --> 00:12:19,324
I meant someone to drink Dr Pepper with.

640
00:12:19,324 --> 00:12:20,704
Just that?

641
00:12:20,704 --> 00:12:22,534
Just that exactly.

642
00:12:22,874 --> 00:12:26,254
We can share in the intellectual experience that is Dr Pepper...

643
00:12:26,254 --> 00:12:31,124
Stop trying to look at my card, while you're saying that.

644
00:12:36,004 --> 00:12:37,554
All right, I win.

645
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:39,474
To be honest,

646
00:12:39,474 --> 00:12:43,394
you're not that good at taking the strategic view, Okabe.

647
00:12:43,764 --> 00:12:47,064
You only consider your own strategy,

648
00:12:47,064 --> 00:12:50,854
never thinking about your opponent's plan,

649
00:12:50,854 --> 00:12:52,024
or whether something is a trap...

650
00:12:52,024 --> 00:12:52,734
Wait!

651
00:12:54,574 --> 00:12:55,574
What?

652
00:12:55,824 --> 00:12:57,364
What did you say?

653
00:12:57,364 --> 00:13:00,574
I said you're not good at taking the strategic view.

654
00:13:00,574 --> 00:13:01,534
I-It's true, isn't it?

655
00:13:03,664 --> 00:13:04,994
Before that!

656
00:13:06,084 --> 00:13:07,204
You said Okabe, right?

657
00:13:08,164 --> 00:13:09,914
So what?

658
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:12,214
I'm younger than you, but for someone

659
00:13:12,214 --> 00:13:13,794
I'm not showing respect for...

660
00:13:13,794 --> 00:13:16,044
No!

661
00:13:16,304 --> 00:13:18,094
I am Hououin!

662
00:13:18,094 --> 00:13:21,134
How many times must I tell you, Christina?

663
00:13:22,184 --> 00:13:24,474
From now on, remember to call me Hououin!

664
00:13:24,894 --> 00:13:28,394
Or Kyouma...

665
00:13:35,944 --> 00:13:37,154
Are you crying?

666
00:13:37,154 --> 00:13:38,784
I'm not crying!

667
00:13:38,784 --> 00:13:40,784
I definitely wasn't terrified by a guy

668
00:13:40,784 --> 00:13:42,204
screaming in my face,

669
00:13:42,204 --> 00:13:44,364
so I definitely didn't start crying from relief afterwards!

670
00:13:44,364 --> 00:13:46,124
That's not what happened!

671
00:13:47,134 --> 00:13:50,254
Daru, why is my assistant crying?

672
00:13:50,254 --> 00:13:53,624
She just told you.

673
00:13:56,794 --> 00:14:01,094
And I put this here... Huh?

674
00:14:01,974 --> 00:14:07,764
If this goes here, then this goes here...

675
00:14:09,104 --> 00:14:10,604
Assistant.

676
00:14:10,604 --> 00:14:11,984
I'm not your assistant, but what?

677
00:14:12,354 --> 00:14:15,524
Why don't you head back to the hotel for the night?

678
00:14:15,524 --> 00:14:16,564
It's close, isn't it?

679
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:17,904
Don't worry.

680
00:14:17,904 --> 00:14:19,944
If it doesn't work by morning, I'll head back.

681
00:14:20,404 --> 00:14:22,694
You don't need to talk to your family?

682
00:14:22,694 --> 00:14:24,154
My mom's in America,

683
00:14:24,154 --> 00:14:26,164
and I haven't spoken to my dad in seven years.

684
00:14:26,164 --> 00:14:27,994
So I don't have anyone to contact.

685
00:14:27,994 --> 00:14:31,244
A prodigal perverted genius girl, then.

686
00:14:31,244 --> 00:14:33,214
Stop making it even weirder.

687
00:14:35,294 --> 00:14:36,214
Got it!

688
00:14:37,214 --> 00:14:39,384
Got it!

689
00:14:39,754 --> 00:14:40,634
You did it?

690
00:14:40,634 --> 00:14:42,634
Mission complete second!

691
00:14:42,634 --> 00:14:43,514
So what's the result?

692
00:14:43,514 --> 00:14:45,554
I haven't seen anything yet.

693
00:14:45,554 --> 00:14:47,844
But I got the Z-program...

694
00:14:47,844 --> 00:14:51,064
It says 1973?

695
00:14:51,064 --> 00:14:52,184
Yeah...

696
00:14:52,184 --> 00:14:53,644
When was SERN founded?

697
00:14:53,644 --> 00:14:55,064
1954.

698
00:14:55,464 --> 00:14:57,444
When was the IBN 5100 made?

699
00:14:57,444 --> 00:14:59,564
1975.

700
00:14:59,944 --> 00:15:01,904
SERN gave the IBN 5100

701
00:15:01,904 --> 00:15:05,954
a special programming language, just for this plan?

702
00:15:05,954 --> 00:15:07,614
That's going too far.

703
00:15:07,614 --> 00:15:08,994
But it's possible.

704
00:15:09,294 --> 00:15:12,084
Once we read this report, we'll know, right?

705
00:15:12,544 --> 00:15:15,124
I'm sure its just an old particle physics report,

706
00:15:15,124 --> 00:15:17,424
and nothing to do with conspiracy theories.

707
00:15:17,734 --> 00:15:19,794
A JPEG? Seriously? Screw you!

708
00:15:19,794 --> 00:15:21,634
I can't copy/paste that!

709
00:15:21,634 --> 00:15:23,424
It's not in French?

710
00:15:23,424 --> 00:15:27,344
Um, "Time Control and Its Destruction of History"...

711
00:15:27,644 --> 00:15:30,604
Oh, yeah. Miss Makise can read English.

712
00:15:30,604 --> 00:15:32,224
Well done, assistant!

713
00:15:32,224 --> 00:15:35,984
Everything you did in America was for this moment!

714
00:15:35,984 --> 00:15:37,984
The hell it was.

715
00:15:37,984 --> 00:15:38,734
Let's see...

716
00:15:38,734 --> 00:15:42,654
This, in turn, enables a utopia heading from the past to the future.

717
00:15:42,654 --> 00:15:46,654
The realization of this will be SERN's reason for existence in the 21st century.

718
00:15:46,954 --> 00:15:48,204
A utopia...

719
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:49,614
Dystopia!

720
00:15:49,914 --> 00:15:51,284
No way!

721
00:15:51,284 --> 00:15:53,494
Anyway, show me the rest.

722
00:15:53,494 --> 00:15:54,624
I can try, I guess.

723
00:15:55,124 --> 00:15:58,294
Hmm... For security reasons, this experiment...

724
00:15:58,294 --> 00:15:59,464
That's not it.

725
00:15:59,464 --> 00:16:00,924
Those engaged by the program...

726
00:16:00,924 --> 00:16:02,294
No, that's not it, either.

727
00:16:02,294 --> 00:16:03,254
Got it.

728
00:16:03,254 --> 00:16:04,594
The Z-program will experiment

729
00:16:04,594 --> 00:16:06,764
with the possibility of transference through space-time,

730
00:16:06,764 --> 00:16:08,554
via high-energy proton collision...

731
00:16:09,844 --> 00:16:12,224
Space-time travel...

732
00:16:12,684 --> 00:16:14,394
They're talking about time travel!

733
00:16:14,394 --> 00:16:15,224
No way!

734
00:16:15,224 --> 00:16:16,484
It's true!

735
00:16:16,484 --> 00:16:21,104
I knew it! SERN's been investigating time travel for forty years!

736
